hadiths[50]{hadithnumber,text}:
"844","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): Which Islam is best? He said: “You give food, and you greet those you know and those you do not know.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"845","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: When Allah Almighty created Adam, (ﷺ) he said: Go and greet those - a group of sitting angels - and listen to what they greet you, for it is your greeting and the greeting of your offspring. So he said: Peace be upon you. They said: May Allah’s peace and mercy be upon you, so he added to it: And Allah’s mercy. (Agreed upon) On him).."
"846","On the authority of Abu Amara Al-Baraa bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded us to do seven things: to visit the sick, to follow funerals, to praise the sneezing person, to support the weak, to help the oppressed, to spread greetings and to fulfill oaths. [Agreed upon. This is the wording of one of Al-Bukhari’s narrations]."
"847","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \By Him in Whose Hand is my life! You will not enter Jannah until you believe"," and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I inform you of something which"," if you do"," you will love one another? Promote greetings amongst yourselves.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"848","On the authority of Abu Yusuf Abdullah bin Salam, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “O people, spread peace, feed food, connect with relatives and pray while people are asleep, and you will enter Paradise in peace” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"849","And on the authority of Al-Tufayl bin Abi bin Ka’b, that he used to come to Abdullah bin Omar, and go with him to the market in the morning. He said: When we went to the market in the morning, Abdullah did not pass by a sweeper, nor a shop owner, nor a poor person, nor anyone without greeting him. Al-Tufayl said: I came to Abdullah bin Omar one day, so he asked me to accompany him to the market, so I said to him: What are you doing in the market, when you do not stand to sell, do not ask about the goods, do not bargain with them, and do not sit in the market places? And I say: Sit with us here and we will talk. So he said, O Abu Batn - and Tufayl had a belly - we only go out in the morning for the sake of greeting, so we greet whomever we meet. [Narrated by Malik in Al-Muwatta’ with an authentic chain of transmission]."
"850","On the authority of Imran bin Al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: Peace be upon you, and he replied to him, then he sat down. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Ten.” Then another came and said: May Allah’s peace and mercy be upon you. He replied to him and he sat down, and the Prophet said: “Twenty.” Then another came and said: May Allah’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon you. He replied to him, so he sat down, and the Prophet said: “Thirty” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"851","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: “This is Gabriel reciting peace to you.” She said: I said: “And upon him be peace, Allah’s mercy, and His blessings” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] And thus it occurred in some of the narrations of the two Sahihs: “And His blessings,” and in some of them, by deleting it and adding trust, it is accepted."
"852","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that if the Prophet (ﷺ) spoke a word, he would repeat it three times until it was understood, and if he came to a people and greeted them, he would greet them three times. [Narrated by al-Bukhari] This applies when the crowd is large."
"853","On the authority of Al-Miqdad, may Allah be pleased with him, in his long hadith, he said: We used to give the Prophet (ﷺ) his share of milk, and Gabriel would come to him at night with a salutation that would not wake a sleeping person, and the awake ones would hear it. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) came and greeted Gabriel as Gabriel used to greet him. [Muslim]."
"854","On the authority of Asmaa bint Yazid, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by the mosque one day, and a group of women were sitting, so he turned his hand in greeting. [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"855","On the authority of Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The most worthy of people in Allah is the one who initiates the greeting of peace with them” [Narrated by Abu Dawud with a good chain of transmission, and Al-Tirmidhi narrated it in a similar way and said: A good hadith, and it was mentioned after him]."
"856","On the authority of Abu Jari al-Hujaimi, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Do not say peace be upon you, for upon you peace is the greeting of the dead.” [Narrated by Abu Dawud and al-Tirmidhi and said: A good and authentic hadith. Its length has already been mentioned]."
"857","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The rider greets the walker, the walker greets the sitting, and the small greets the large.” (Agreed upon) And in a narration by Al-Bukhari: “And the small greets the large.”"
"858","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \The person nearest to Allah is one who is the first to offer greeting.\"" [Abu Dawud"," with a sound chain] . The narration in At-Tirmidhi is: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: \""O Messenger of Allah! When two persons meet"," who should greet the other first?'' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""The person nearest to Allah (i.e."," one who is more obedient and therefore closer to Allah will say: As-Salam first).\"""""
"859","He came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and greeted him. The Prophet (ﷺ) responded to the greeting and said, \Go back and repeat your Salat because you have not performed the Salat (properly).'' He again performed Salat as he had prayed before and came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and greeted him. The Prophet (ﷺ) responded to the greetings (and repeated his words to him). This act of repeating (the Salat and the Salam) was done thrice. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"860","And on his authority, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “If one of you meets his brother, let him greet him. If a tree, wall, or stone comes between them, and then he meets him, let him greet him.” [Abu Dawud]."
"861","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: “O my son, if you enter upon your family and greet them, it will be a blessing upon you and upon your household” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"862","\Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do the same.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"863","On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: There was a woman among us - and in one narration: We had an old woman - who would take some of the roots of Swiss chard and throw it into the pot, and crush the grains of barley. When we prayed the Friday prayer and left, we would greet her, and she would bring it to us. [Al-Bukhari]."
"864","I went to the Prophet (ﷺ) on the day of the conquest of Makkah. He was taking a bath and Fatimah was screening him with a cloth. I greeted him. And she mentioned the rest of the Hadith. [Muslim] ."
"865","The Prophet (ﷺ) passed by us when we were with a party of women, and he greeted us with salam. [Abu Dawud and At-Tirmidhi who classified it as Hasan] . This is the wording of Abu Dawud. In At-Tirmidhi: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed through the Masjid one day, and a group of women were sitting, so he motioned his hand with the salam."
"866","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Do not greet the Jews and the Christians before they greet you; and when you meet any one of them on the road"," force him to go to the narrowest part of it.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"867","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “When the People of the Book greet you, say: And upon you” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"868","On the authority of Osama, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by a gathering in which there was a mixture of Muslims and polytheists - idol worshipers and Jews - so the Prophet (ﷺ) greeted them” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"869","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If one of you reaches the meeting, let him greet, and if he wants to get up, let him greet, for the first greeting is not more deserving than the last greeting” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"870","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Seeking permission is three times: if he gives you permission, otherwise return” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"871","On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The request for permission was only made for the sake of sight” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"872","On the authority of Rab’i bin Harrash, he said: A man from Banu Amir told us that he asked permission from the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was in a house, and he said: Should I enter? So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to his servant: “Go out to this man and teach him permission, so say to him: Say: Peace be upon you, shall I enter?” The man heard him and said: Peace be upon you, shall I enter? So the Prophet (ﷺ) gave him permission. May Allah grant him peace, so he entered. [Abu Dawud]."
"873","On the authority of Kalada bin Al-Hanbal, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and I entered upon him but did not greet him. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Go back and say, ‘Peace be upon you. Shall I enter?’” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"874","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, in his famous hadith regarding the Night Journey, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Then Gabriel ascended with me to the lowest heaven and asked for the gate to be opened. It was said: Who is this? He said: Gabriel. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. Then he ascended to the second, third, fourth and all the rest of the heavens, and it is said at the door of each heaven: Who is this? He says: Gabriel” (Agreed upon)."
"875","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: One night I went out and saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) walking alone. So I started walking in the shadow of the moon, and he turned and saw me and said: “Who is this?” I said: Abu Dharr, [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"876","I went to the Prophet (ﷺ) who was taking a bath while Fatimah was screening him. He asked, \Who is there?\"" I replied: \""I am Umm Hani.\"" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"877","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and I knocked on the door, and he said, “Who is it?” So I said: Me, and he said: “Me? Me?!” As if he disliked that (the manner of his address) [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"878","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \Allah likes sneezing and dislikes yawning. When any one of you sneezes and says `Al-hamdu lillah (praise be to Allah)'"," it becomes obligatory upon every Muslim who hears him to respond with `Yarhamuk-Allah (may Allah have mercy on you)'. Yawning is from the devil. When one of you feels like yawning"," he should restrain it as much as possible"," for the devil laughs when one of you yawns.\"" [Al-Bukhari] ."""
"879","On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah; and let his brother or companions say to him: May Allah have mercy on you. And if he says to him: May Allah have mercy on you, let him say: May Allah guide you and put your affairs in order.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"880","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “If one of you sneezes and praises Allah, then respond to him with 'May Allah have mercy on you', but if he does not praise Allah, do not respond to him with that” [Muslim]."
"881","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet (ﷺ) and he responded to the sneeze of one of them and did not respond to the other. The one who did not smell it said: So-and-so sneezed and you responded to him, and I sneezed and you did not respond to me? So he said: “This is because he praised Allah, but you did not praise Allah” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"882","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sneezed, he would put his hand or his garment on it, and lower - or suppress - his voice with it. The narrator doubted. [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"883","The Jews used to intentionally sneeze in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) hoping that he would say to them: 'Yarhamukum-ullah (may Allah have mercy on you),' but he would respond with: \Yahdikum-ullahu wa yuslihu balakum (may Allah guide you and render sound your state of affairs).\"" [Abu Dawud and At- Tirmidhi] ."""
"884","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If one of you yawns, let him hold his hand over his mouth, for Satan will enter” [Muslim]."
"885","On the authority of Abu Al-Khattab Qatada, he said: I said to Anas: Was the handshake among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)? He said: Yes” [Al-Bukhari]."
"886","When the people of Yemen came, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \The people of Yemen have visited you. They are the first to introduce the tradition of handshaking.\"" [Abu Dawud] ."""
"887","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Two Muslims will not meet and shake hands without having their sins forgiven (by Allah ) before they depart.\"" [Abu Dawud] ."""
"888","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man among us meets his brother or friend. Should he bow to him? He said: “No.” He said: “Should he stick to him and kiss him?” He said: “No.” He said: So he takes his hand and shakes it? He said: “Yes” ([Al-Tirmidhi]."
"889","On the authority of Safwan bin Assal, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A Jew said to his friend: Take us to this Prophet (ﷺ). They came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and asked him about nine clear signs. So he mentioned the hadith to his saying: So they kissed his hand and foot, and said: We bear witness that you are a prophet. [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"890","And on the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, a story in which he said: “Then we approached the Prophet (ﷺ) and we kissed his hand” [Abu Dawud]."
"891","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Zaid bin Haritha came to Medina and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to my house. He came to him and knocked on the door, and the Prophet (ﷺ) stood up to him, dragging his garment, so he embraced him and kissed him. [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"892","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: “Do not despise any good deed, even if it is meeting your brother with a cheerful face” [Muslim]."
"893","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) kissed Al-Hasan bin Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, and Al-Aqra’ bin Habis said: I have ten children and I have not kissed any of them. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He who does not have mercy will not be shown mercy!” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
